Kc5 Rh5+ 68. Kd4 Rh4+ 69. Ke5 Rh5+ {... four more moves are recorded by
Tinsley but he makes a hash of the notation. It runs... 70.K-K6 R-R3ch 71.R-B6
R-Rsq 72.K-Q6 R-Ktsq 73.K-K7 Resigns. Makes no sense - possibly the game ended
something like} 70. Kf6 Rh6+ 71. Rg6 Rh8 72. Ke6 Re8+ 73. Kd7 1-0

